API-21: skip de-activated controls when choosing the time step

EN_setcontrol de-activates a control by setting its link index to 0.
controls() skips such controls, but controltimestep() did not: it still
shortened the hydraulic time step to the control's trigger time, and
compared the control's status with that of the unused link slot 0.
Skip controls with a link index of 0 there too.

Apply from the root of an EPANET checkout at 83e25bb:
    git apply API-21_fix.patch

diff --git a/src/hydraul.c b/src/hydraul.c
index fa96868..c4778b3 100755
--- a/src/hydraul.c
+++ b/src/hydraul.c
@@ -763,6 +763,10 @@ int  controltimestep(Project *pr, long *tstep)
         {
             continue;
         }
+
+        // Skip a control de-activated by setting its link to 0
+        if (control->Link <= 0) continue;
+
         // Control depends on a tank level
         if ( (n = control->Node) > 0)
         {
